# Everything the dashboard image must never see.
#
# `node_modules` and `.next` are the important two: both are large, both are
# regenerated inside the build, and a host copy of either would be wrong for
# the image's platform. `.env*` matters for a different reason — a developer's
# real configuration must not be copied into a layer.

node_modules/
.next/
out/
coverage/
.turbo/

# Local configuration. `.env.example` is kept: it is documentation, holds no
# secret, and the README refers to it.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Key material, for the same reason the repository-root .dockerignore excludes
# it. Nothing in this build reads a certificate or a private key, so a stray
# one in the working tree can only leak into a layer.
*.pem
*.key

# Build and editor artefacts
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts
.DS_Store
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# Docker's own files: nothing in the image reads them.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
